  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "De Morgan's law for disjunctions states that the negation of a disjunction of two statements is equivalent to the conjunction of the negations of the individual statements. It can be stated symbolically as follows:\n\n$$\n¬(A∨B)=¬A∧¬B\n$$\n\nSo, the negation of our statement is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(10\\text{ is odd}\\text{ or }10\\,|\\,50) & ≡¬((10\\text{ is odd})∨(10\\,|\\,50)) \\\\  & ≡¬(10\\text{ is odd})∧¬(10\\,|\\,50) \\\\  & ≡(10\\text{ is even})∧(10\\,\\text{⧸}|\\,50) \\\\  & ≡10\\text{ is even}\\text{ and }10\\,\\text{⧸}|\\,50.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
